# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Paths into user-writable or package-manager folders that may remain in the engine, and why each
# is harmless. tools/path-scan.py reads this; package.sh fails on any hit not matched here.
# Format (tab separated): file glob (relative to the engine root)  regular expression  reason
# Keep this list short: a new line needs a reason someone can check in the source.
lib/wine/aarch64-unix/ntdll.so	^/tmp/\.wine-%u/server-%llx-%llx$	Wine's wineserver socket folder (dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c). Created by Wine with mode 0700; client and server stop unless it is a directory owned by the user with no group or other access (server/request.c create_dir). Runtime IPC, not a file Wine loads code or data from.
bin/wineserver	^/tmp/\.wine-%u$	The same socket folder, server side (server/request.c), with the same ownership and mode checks.
bin/wineserver	^/usr/local/share/wine/nls$	Last-resort read-only fallbacks for l_intl.nls (server/unicode.c load_intl_file), tried only if the engine's own share/wine/nls/l_intl.nls (shipped) cannot be opened. A case-mapping data table, opened O_RDONLY; no code.
lib/wine/aarch64-unix/crypt32.so	^/usr/local/share/certs/$	Read-only fallback root-certificate folder (dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c), used only if the macOS keychain (SecTrustSettingsCopyCertificates, read first) returns no root certificate at all.
lib/wine/*-windows/dbghelp.dll	^/usr/local/lib:/lib:/usr/lib$	dbghelp's default search path for unix debug symbols (dlls/dbghelp/macho_module.c), used only when a debugger asks for symbols of a host library; reads them, never runs them.
lib/wine/*-windows/winemenubuilder.exe	^/usr/local/share/:/usr/share/$	XDG_DATA_DIRS default of winemenubuilder (Linux desktop menus); the engine turns winemenubuilder off (WINEDLLOVERRIDES winemenubuilder.exe=d) and it only reads there.
lib/wine/*-windows/wineps.drv	^/tmpmtrx matrix def$	Not a path: PostScript source text in the printer driver ("/tmpmtrx" is a PostScript name).
lib/wine/aarch64-windows/*fex.dll	^/tmp/perf-\{\}\.map$	FEX's JIT symbol map (FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp), written only when a FEX JIT-naming debug option is turned on (off by default); inside a Windows DLL the path resolves inside the Wine prefix (C:\tmp\...), not on the Mac.
lib/wine/aarch64-windows/xtajit*.dll	^/tmp/perf-\{\}\.map$	The same FEX DLLs under the names Wine loads them by.
lib/wine/aarch64-windows/*fex.dll	^/Users/runner/work/llvm-mingw/llvm-mingw/llvm-project/(libcxxabi|libunwind)/src/	__FILE__ strings inside libc++abi and libunwind, which llvm-mingw's release built on GitHub's CI (user "runner") and FEX links statically: text of assertion and abort messages ("%s:%d: %s", "libunwind: ..."), never opened. Not a path on any Mac; rebuilding llvm-mingw's runtime is the only way to change it.
lib/wine/aarch64-windows/xtajit*.dll	^/Users/runner/work/llvm-mingw/llvm-mingw/llvm-project/(libcxxabi|libunwind)/src/	The same, in the copies Wine loads.
